{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPLEMENTED — Gerrit change 1186 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1186), commit\ne62afec98e, based on main 46dae1a5aa.\n\n=== WHAT THIS TICKET TURNED OUT TO BE ===\nIts ORIGINAL scope — two drifted copies of the local->Jira maps inside `adapters/jira/` — was\nalready delivered by story J2 [rebar:62d9-9f6d-ecf4-4743], verified against the tree rather than\nassumed: `adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py` is now the sole adapter-side definition, the ACLI\ntransport reads it (`acli.py:73,75`; `acli_cli_ops.py:35`) and so does the Backend port\n(`outbound_fields.py:35-36`), and the `deleted` drift is decided (`\"Done\"`) and pinned by\n`test_acli_status_resolution_heldout.py`. Three of the four original ACs were met.\nThe residue is the THIRD copy, which J2 deliberately left out of scope and named this ticket for\nin its own module docstring: \"``rebar_reconciler/config.py``'s separate third copy is deliberately\nout of this story's scope — see bug fe15-3bc4-ed70-4b61.\" The plan was rewritten to that residue\nbefore review, and PASSED FIRST TRY.\n\n=== THE GAP, MEASURED ===\n`config.local_to_jira_status` is content-identical to `LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` today (compared\nprogrammatically: `==` is True), so there is no drift YET. Nothing prevented one. Mutating\n`config.local_to_jira_status[\"deleted\"]` to `\"Archived-MUTANT\"` — not a state in the live DIG\nworkflow — left **59 tests GREEN** across `state/test_config.py`,\n`test_acli_status_resolution_heldout.py`, `test_jira_family_seam.py` and\n`test_jira_family_boundary_heldout.py`.\n\n=== THE FIX, AND WHY IT IS A TEST RATHER THAN AN IMPORT ===\nA parity test plus a lock-step comment — NOT single-sourcing via an import. `config.py` imports\nnothing but `__future__`, and `adapters/jira_family` declares a one-way dependency direction\n(\"concrete backends import this package; it never imports them back\"), so importing the adapter\ninto core would invert that layering and put the operator-override surface — including the\ndocumented empty-dict kill-switch — behind an adapter import.\nThis is the idiom the file ALREADY uses for the same problem one map over:\n`config.jira_to_local_status` is a second literal of `inbound_differ._JIRA_TO_LOCAL_STATUS`, kept\nhonest by `test_jira_to_local_status_parity_with_inbound_differ` plus a comment saying so. The new\ntest mirrors it, and the new comment mirrors that comment's form.\n\n=== AC-BY-AC ===\n[full-dict equality via a by-path load] `test_local_to_jira_status_parity_with_the_jira_family_map`\nasserts `config.local_to_jira_status == value_maps.LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA`. Full dict, not a spot\ncheck — the existing idea-across-all-maps test already pins ONE key (`idea`), and the other six\nwere the unguarded ones, which is why the mutation went unseen.\n[MUTATION-CHECKED, both verdicts] With `\"deleted\"` mutated: **1 failed, 59 passed** — the new test\nfails naming the drift, and it is the ONLY failure. Reverted: **60 passed**.\n[lock-step comment naming the canonical map and the enforcing test] Added above\n`local_to_jira_status`, in the same form as the existing `jira_to_local_status` comment.\n[config.py still imports nothing outside `__future__`] Verified: `grep '^import\\|^from'` returns\nonly `from __future__ import annotations`.\n[kill-switch and override unchanged; only an ADDED test] `git diff --numstat`: test_config.py\n53 added / 0 deleted; config.py 12 added / 0 deleted. Zero deleted lines in either file, so no\nexisting test was edited and no behaviour changed — the change is a comment and a test.\n[all four suites pass] 60 passed.\n\n=== NOT DONE, DELIBERATELY ===\nNo map VALUES changed (they already agree; changing one would be a behaviour change this ticket\ndoes not need), and the priority map is untouched because `config.py` has NO priority copy —\nverified: the module exposes no priority attribute at all, so there is no third priority literal\nto pin.\n\nGATES: `make lint` and `make typecheck` both pass. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785623911216225001,"uuid":"9966e746-7bac-4113-865e-e942034300b1"}